# Configured channels are in the sidebar before anything connects. After 001
# they are joined in two lines, unkeyed and then keyed, with the keys in the
# order of their channels. A channel the server refuses stays parted and
# waiting (Textual only uses its join-error flag to skip a KICK rejoin), so
# the next link tries it again; the server's own spelling of a name finds
# the configured channel's buffer.
= autojoin #A #B #c:key1 #d:key2
! connect
> dial #1 irc.test:6667 plain
? notice Connecting to irc.test:6667
? buffers = console #A #B #c #d
? parted #A
? rejoin #A on-connect
? rejoin #d on-connect
! opened
> CAP LS 302
> NICK textual
> USER textual 0 * Textual
< :irc.test 001 textual :Welcome
> JOIN #A,#B
> JOIN #c,#d key1,key2
? registered textual
? parted #A
< :textual!u@h JOIN #a
> MODE #a
? joined #A
? buffers = console #A #B #c #d
< :irc.test 474 textual #B :Cannot join channel (+b)
? line console Message(474): #B Cannot join channel (+b)
? parted #B
? rejoin #B on-connect
< :textual!u@h JOIN #c
> MODE #c
< :textual!u@h JOIN #d
> MODE #d
? joined #d
! closed eof
? notice Disconnected: the server closed the connection; reconnecting in 5 s
? rejoin #A on-connect
? rejoin #B on-connect
? rejoin #d on-connect
@ wake
> dial #2 irc.test:6667 plain
? notice Connecting to irc.test:6667
! opened
> CAP LS 302
> NICK textual
> USER textual 0 * Textual
< :irc.test 001 textual :Welcome
> JOIN #A,#B
> JOIN #c,#d key1,key2
? registered textual
